Lyrics:
[Verse 1]
Hannah can make music here,
Hannah can make music there,
Hannah can make music absolutely anywhere.

She'll make it in a Walmart,
she'll make it in a store,
she'll make it in a hurricane —
and then she'll make some more.

[Chorus]
Oh Hannah, oh Hannah,
the songs just keep on pouring,
in a basket, on a rooftop,
while the thunderclouds are roaring.
She'll hum it to her dogs,
she'll whisper it at night,
she'll write it in her bedroom
by the soft iphone light.

[Verse 2]
She'll make it eating s'mores,
she'll make it on the floor,
she'll make it at Micro Center
with the buzzing of the door.

She'll make it when she's tired,
she'll make it when she's wired,
she'll make it when she swears
she's absolutely too retired.

[Chorus]
Oh Hannah, oh Hannah,
the songs just keep on pouring,
in a basket, on a rooftop,
while the thunderclouds are roaring.
She'll sing it to a squirrel,
she'll sing it to the moon,
she'll sing it in the morning
and again by afternoon.

[Bridge — playful, almost spoken]
Some folks need a quiet room,
some folks need a grand piano,
some folks need a symphony
or an opera in Milano.

But Hannah?
Hannah just needs Hannah.
And maybe a banana.

[Final Chorus — bigger, with claps]
Oh Hannah, oh Hannah,
the world is full of songs,
and most of them are hiding
where they figure they belong.
But Hannah goes and finds them
in the strangest little nooks —
in hurricanes and hallways
and the margins of her books.

[Outro — soft, smiling]
So if you ever wonder
where the next one's gonna be —
just look for Hannah humming
in a place you'd never see.

(That's where she'll be.)